id: 19
hanzi: 结论
pinyin: jié lùn
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: conclusion; final verdict; outcome; logical deduction drawn from premises
  es: conclusión; veredicto final; deducción lógica; dictamen razonado

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a final judgment, verdict, or deduction reached after reasoning, investigation, or experimentation | juicio final, dictamen o deducción razonada a la que se llega tras indagar, deliberar o investigar | 得出结论 (reach a conclusion)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 经过数月严密细致的对照实验，科研小组终于得出了令人信服的实验结论。 | Jīngguò shù yuè yánmì xìzhì de duìzhào shíyàn, kēyán xiǎozǔ zhōngyú déchū le lìngrén xìnfú de shíyàn jiélùn. | After months of rigorous and meticulous controlled trials, the research team finally reached a compelling experimental conclusion. | Tras meses de minuciosos y rigurosos ensayos de control, el equipo científico alcanzó al fin una conclusión experimental convincente.
  #2 | 盲人们摸到大象身体的不同部位便匆忙下结论，结果谁的答案都不准确，这启示我们调查研究切不可仓促武断。 | Mángrénmen mōdào dàxiàng shēntǐ de bùtóng bùwèi biàn cōngmáng xià jiélùn, jiéguǒ shuí de dá'àn dōu bù zhǔnquè, zhè qǐshì wǒmen diàochá-yánjiū qiè bùkě cāngcù wǔduàn. | The blind men rushed to conclusions after touching different parts of the elephant, with none being accurate; this reminds us that investigations must never be hasty or dogmatic. | Los ciegos extrajeron conclusiones apresuradas tras palpar partes distintas del animal, errando todos; ello enseña que ninguna indagación debe ser precipitada ni dogmática.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  得出结论 | reach or draw a conclusion
  下结论 | jump to or pass a conclusion
  最终结论 | final conclusion; definitive verdict
  科学结论 | scientific conclusion
  过早下结论 | draw premature conclusions
  验证结论 | verify or validate a conclusion

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  盖棺定论 | gài guān dìng lùn | pass final verdict on a person's life only after the coffin lid is sealed
  盖棺论定 | gài guān lùn dìng | final judgment is made after death
  不根之论 | bù gēn zhī lùn | groundless statement; unfounded opinion
  长篇大论 | cháng piān dà lùn | long-winded speech or writing; lengthy harangue

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  结 | jié | tie knot; bind; crystallize; fruit | atar; anudar; fructificar; cuajar | 纟 | silk / thread | 纟 (silk thread, knotting cords) | 吉 (jí, auspicious / lucky) | 9 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: silk thread 纟 tied into an auspicious knot 吉, signifying sealing, binding, or bearing firm fruit. | Weaving strong silk threads (纟) into an auspicious, unbreakable knot (吉) binds the final outcome (结). | Trenzar hebras de seda (纟) en un lazo de buena ventura (吉) anuda y sella el resultado definitivo (结). | 35 | VMGR | 結
  论 | lùn | discuss; discourse; theory; evaluate | discutir; opinar; teoría; tratado | 讠 | speech / words | 讠 (speech, verbal deliberation) | 仑 (lún, bamboo scrolls bound in logical order) | 6 | 左右结构 | Simplified from 論. Words 讠 deliberating upon bamboo tablets bound in orderly scrolls 仑, denoting reasoned discourse. | Articulating spoken words (讠) according to an organized scroll of logic (仑) produces rational discourse (论). | Pronunciar palabras (讠) ateniéndose a un rollo ordenado de argumentos (仑) da vida al razonamiento (论). | 51 | IVOP | 論

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Tying together all the loose threads (结) of a reasoned discourse (论) yields the final logical conclusion (结论).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Atar los cabos sueltos (结) de una argumentación meditada (论) conduce a la conclusión final (结论).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In classical epistemology, 结 represents the solid knot tying together disparate threads of evidence, while 论 represents systematic discourse and debate. Hence 结论 is not an arbitrary opinion, but the bound fruit of exhaustive inquiry.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Rising 2nd tone followed by falling 4th tone: 'jié lùn' (35-51). Lift the vocal pitch smoothly on 'jié' before a sharp, decisive downward strike on 'lùn'.

